esize grow width 10px-    bindsym Up resize shrink height 10px-    bindsym Down resize grow height 10px-    bindsym Left resize shrink width 10px-    # Ditto, with arrow keys--    bindsym $right resize grow width 10px-    bindsym $up resize shrink height 10px-    bindsym $down resize grow height 10px-    bindsym $left resize shrink width 10px-    # down will grow the containers height-    # up will shrink the containers height-    # right will grow the containers width-    # left will shrink the containers width-mode "resize" {# Resizing containers:## bindsym $mod+minus scratchpad show## If there are multiple scratchpad windows, this command cycles through them.# Show the next scratchpad window or hide the focused scratchpad window.# bindsym $mod+Shift+minus move scratchpad## Move the currently focused window to the scratchpad# You can send windows there and get them back later.# Sway has a "scratchpad", which is a bag of holding for windows.## Scratchpad:## bindsym $mod+a focus parent# Move focus to the parent container# bindsym $mod+space focus mode_toggle# Swap focus between the tiling area and the floating areabindsym $mod+Shift+f floating toggle# Toggle the current focus between tiling and floating modebindsym $mod+f fullscreen# Make the current focus fullscreenbindsym $mod+z layout toggle splitbindsym $mod+w layout tabbedbindsym $mod+s layout stacking# Switch the current container between different layout stylesbindsym $mod+v splitvbindsym $mod+b splith# respectively.# $mod+b or $mod+v, for horizontal and vertical splits# You can "split" the current object of your focus with## Layout stuff:######## ##     ##    ##     #######   #######     ####       ##     ##    ##    ##     ## ##     ##    ####       #########    ##    ##     ## ##     ##    ####       ##     ##    ##    ##     ## ##     ##    ####        ##   ##    ####   ##     ## ##     ##    ####         ## ##    ##  ##  ##     ## ##     ##    ####          ###    ##    ##  #######  ##     ## ########assign [app_id="google-chrome"] "1"assign [app_id="Slack"] "4"assign [app_id="librewolf"] "2"# Assignations# We just use 1-10 as the default.# Note: workspaces can have any name you want, not just numbers.bindsym $mod+Shift+0 move container to workspace number 10bindsym $mod+Shift+9 move container to workspace number 9bindsym $mod+Shift+8 move container to workspace number 8bindsym $mod+Shift+7 move container to workspace number 7bindsym $mod+Shift+6 move container to workspace number 6bindsym $mod+Shift+5 move container to workspace number 5bindsym $mod+Shift+4 move container to workspace number 4bindsym $mod+Shift+3 move container to workspace number 3bindsym $mod+Shift+2 move container to workspace number 2bindsym $mod+Shift+1 move container to workspace number 1# Move focused container to workspacebindsym $mod+0 workspace number 10bindsym $mod+9 workspace number 9bindsym $mod+8 workspace number 8bindsym $mod+7 workspace number 7bindsym $mod+6 workspace number 6bindsym $mod+5 workspace number 5bindsym $mod+4 workspace number 4bindsym $mod+3 workspace number 3bindsym $mod+2 workspace number 2bindsym $mod+1 workspace number 1# Switch to workspace## Workspaces: ###  ###   #######  ##     ## ##    ##  ######  ##        ##     ##  ######  ########  ########  ##  ## ##     ## ##    ##  ##   ##  ##    ## ##        ##     ## ##    ## ##       ##    ####  ##  ## ##     ## ##   ##   ##  ##         ## ##        ######### ##       ##             ####  ##  ## ##     ## ########  #####     ######  ########  ##     ## ##       ######    ########  ##  ## ##     ## ##     ## ##  ##   ##       ##     ##  ##   ##  ##       ##       ####  ##  ## ##     ## ##     ## ##   ##  ##    ## ##     ##   ## ##   ##    ## ##       ##    ####      ##  #######  ########  ##    ##  ######  ########     ###     ######  ########  ######bindsym $mod+Shift+Right move rightbindsym $mod+Shift+Up move upbindsym $mod+Shift+Down move downbindsym $mod+Shift+Left move left# Ditto, with arrow keysbindsym $mod+Shift+$right move rightbindsym $mod+Shift+$up move upbindsym $mod+Shift+$down move downbindsym $mod+Shift+$left move left# Move the focused window with the same, but add Shiftbindsym $mod+Right focus rightbindsym $mod+Up focus upbindsym $mod+Down focus downbindsym $mod+Left focus left# Or use $mod+[up|down|left|right]bindsym $mod+$right focus rightbindsym $mod+$up focus upbindsym $mod+$down focus downbindsym $mod+$left focus left# Move your focus around## Moving around:##    ## ########    ##     ########     ## ##     ##   ## ##    ##  ##   ### ##    ####     ## ##     ## ##     ##  ##  ##  #### ##    #### ### ## ##     ## ##     ##  ##  ## ## ## ##   ######## #### ##     ## ##     ##  ##  ####  ## #####   ### ##     ## ##     ##  ##  ###   ## ##    ####     ##  #######  ##     ## #### ##    ##  ######bindsym $mod+e exec nautilusbindsym Print exec ~/bin/screenshotbindsym $mod+Control+Space exec ~/bin/shortcutsbindsym $mod+Shift+Space exec ~/bin/bookmarksbindsym $mod+Space exec ~/bin/rofillobindsym $mod+Return exec $term# Programs    -B 'Yes, exit sway' 'swaymsg exit'    -m 'You pressed the exit shortcut. Do you really want to exit sway? This will end your Wayland session.' \bindsym $mod+Shift+e exec swaynag -t warning \# Exit sway (logs you out of your Wayland session)bindsym $mod+Shift+r reload# Reload the configuration filefloating_modifier $mod normal# mouse button for dragging.# Change normal to inverse to use left mouse button for resizing and right# Despite the name, also works for non-floating windows.# Resize them with right mouse button + $mod.# Drag floating windows by holding down $mod and left mouse button.# bindsym $mod+d exec dmenu_run# Start your launcherbindsym $mod+Shift+w kill# Kill focused window## Basics:#### Key bindings##    ## ########    ##     ########   ##  ##          ##    ##    ####  ##   ##          ##          #######    ######      ##     ########  ##   ##         ####   ####   ##  ##        ##  ##  ##    ####    ## ######## ##    ##  ######}    xkb_options ctrl:nocaps    xkb_variant altgr-intl    xkb_layout usinput "type:keyboard" {}    middle_emulation enabled    natural_scroll enabled    tap enabled    dwt enabledinput "1739:53259:VEN_06CB:00_06CB:D00B_Touchpad" {# Read `man 5 sway-input` for more information about this section.# You can get the names of your inputs by running: swaymsg -t get_inputs##   }#       middle_emulation enabled#       natural_scroll enabled#       tap enabled#       dwt enabled#   input "2:14:SynPS/2_Synaptics_TouchPad" {## Example configuration:#### Input configuration#### ##    ## ##         #######     ## ##  ##   ### ##        ##     ##    ## ##  ##  #### ##        ##     ##    ## ##  ## ## ## ########  ##     ##    ## ##  ####  ## ##     ## ##     ##    ## ##  ###   ## ##     ## ##     ##    ###### ##    ## ########  ##     ## ######### resumed. It will also lock your screen before your computer goes to sleep.# your displays after another 300 seconds, and turn your screens back on when# This will lock your screen after 300 seconds of inactivity, then turn off##          before-sleep 'swaylock -f -c 000000'#          timeout 600 'swaymsg "output * power off"' resume 'swaymsg "output * power on"' \#          timeout 300 'swaylock -f -c 000000' \# exec swayidle -w \## Example configuration:#### Idle configuration# output eDP-1 enable# output * disable# Managed by kanshi profiles, see ~/.config/kanshi/config# You can get the names of your outputs by running: swaymsg -t get_outputs##   output HDMI-A-1 resolution 1920x1080 position 1920,0## Example configuration:#output * bg /home/luis/Pictures/pixel-space-wallpapers.png fill# output * bg /usr/share/backgrounds/sway/Sway_Wallpaper_Blue_1920x1080.png fill# Default wallpaper (more resolutions are available in /usr/share/backgrounds/sway/)#### Output configuration #######   #######     ##    ##         #######     ####     ## ##     ##    ##    ##        ##     ##    ####     ## ##     ##    ##    ##        ##     ##    ####     ## ##     ##    ##    ########  ##     ##    ####     ## ##     ##    ##    ##     ## ##     ##    ####     ## ##     ##    ##    ##     ## ##     ##    ## #######  ##     ## ######## ########  ##     ## ########include /etc/sway/config-vars.d/*set $menu dmenu_path | wmenu | xargs swaymsg exec --# on the original workspace that the command was run on.# Note: pass the final command to swaymsg so that the resulting window can be opened# Your preferred application launcherset $term foot# Your preferred terminal emulatorset $right lset $up kset $down jset $left h# Home row direction keys, like vimset $mod Mod4# Logo key. Use Mod1 for Alt.#### Variables# Read `man 5 sway` for a complete reference.## Copy this to ~/.config/sway/config and edit it to your liking.##
# Copy this to ~/.config/sway/config and edit it to your liking.
#
# Read `man 5 sway` for a complete reference.

### Variables
#
# Logo key. Use Mod1 for Alt.
set $mod Mod4
# Home row direction keys, like vim
set $left h
set $down j
set $up k
set $right l
# Your preferred terminal emulator
set $term foot
# Your preferred application launcher
# Note: pass the final command to swaymsg so that the resulting window can be opened
# on the original workspace that the command was run on.
set $menu dmenu_path | wmenu | xargs swaymsg exec --

include /etc/sway/config-vars.d/*

 #######  ##     ## ######## ########  ##     ## ########
